00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:36.800
do anything."

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:38.720
Baby, I can't imagine that life for

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.960
myself. And I'd rather work hard and be

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:42.400
free than be well-rested all the time

00:09:40.960 --> 00:09:44.160
and have nothing on my own. I don't mean

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:46.240
to say that to shame anyone who's in

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:48.320
this situation. I say it because I want

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:50.120
you to see the trade-off. There is

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.800
always a trade-off. And if you want

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:53.720
something like that for yourself, I want

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:55.600
you to see that and see all of sides to

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:57.240
it before you go and make that decision

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:59.200
for yourself. And then you're in that

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.920
situation, what do you have that is

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.840
yours and what are you building that is

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:04.720
your own? Because you can always rest.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:06.720
It's always a part of the equation. It's

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.560
always, you know, something that is

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:10.480
offered to us. We're all entitled to

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:13.160
rest, but you cannot always leave our

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:14.600
situation later. Everything is a tool. I

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:16.520
want to be nuanced [music] in the way

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:19.040
that I say this because it can be

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:21.360
misinterpreted, but everything in your

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:23.120
life that you encounter is a tool,

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:25.960
whether it's a person, a job

00:10:23.120 --> 00:10:27.880
opportunity, or room that you walk into.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:29.600
I'm not saying to use anyone [music] and

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:31.360
to bleed them dry, okay? I'm not saying

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.760
to be transactional or have these kinds

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:34.840
of relationships or to be cold to

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:36.280
everyone. That is not my point at all.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:38.320
I'm saying that most people walk through

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:40.280
their lives waiting and waiting to be

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:41.480
given something, or they constantly want

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:43.720
something and they will wait until they

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:45.200
get it. But then the people who walk

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:47.040
free, they actually walk through their

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.360
lives recognizing [music] what's already

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.240
been offered to them, what they have

00:10:48.360 --> 00:10:52.520
access to, and they take that

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:54.560
opportunity. They take it. There's a big

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:57.640
difference between just constant

00:10:54.560 --> 00:10:58.920
extraction and recognition, recognizing

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:00.200
that all these people living their dream

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:01.440
lives that I've met this summer, for

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:03.160
example, in Europe, they're not more

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:04.440
talented than you. They're not richer

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:05.839
than you when they first started,

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:07.760
especially the couple who I spoke to

00:11:05.839 --> 00:11:09.560
with that amazing guest house. They had

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:10.727
nothing when they first got married and

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.000
they built everything,

00:11:10.727 --> 00:11:12.640
>> [music]

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:14.280
>> you know, after that. They just

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:15.600
basically looked around them and what

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:18.200
was around and they asked a different

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:21.080
question to benefit themselves and not

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:23.200
just, "Why doesn't anyone help me?" But,

00:11:21.080 --> 00:11:25.280
"What is right here, right now, that I

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:27.120
can actually use?" For example, that

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.640
Greek guy that I met, Greece, for

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:30.377
example, does not have a strong economy.

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:31.400
A lot of people know this. And a part

00:11:30.377 --> 00:11:33.160
[music] of what makes me feel great

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:34.480
about doing my group trips in Greece is

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:36.720
that I'm helping a lot of small

00:11:34.480 --> 00:11:38.800
businesses, locals. We all get to meet

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:41.200
the owners, we get to talk to them every

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:43.240
day, and we directly contribute to their

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:45.480
success instead of some faceless

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:47.480
billionaire conglomerates. But, yeah, I

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:49.240
mean, I met Greeks there who are doing

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:52.040
very well because they looked at what

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:54.120
Greece does have: islands, tourism,

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:56.000
beauty, seasons. And they built around

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:57.600
that. And in fact, I think that recently

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:59.200
Greece was voted the most beautiful

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:02.200
country in the world for the year of

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:04.400
2026 But then, also like meanwhile, I've

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:06.120
also talked to people who have far more

00:12:04.400 --> 00:12:08.480
things available to them, including

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:09.800
people who make a ton of money, and they

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:11.960
will always end up with nothing, and

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:14.240
their whole internal monologue is, "This

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:15.720
costs too much. I can't have anything. I

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:16.840
can't afford to do this or do that. We

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:18.560
can't go anywhere. There's no

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:20.760
opportunity here." For example, and I

00:12:18.560 --> 00:12:22.560
also met a cab driver in Athens who's

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.880
not making like, you know, incredible

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.760
amount of money. And I was just saying

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:26.200
to her like, you know, "Why are you

00:12:24.760 --> 00:12:27.560
driving in Athens? Go to the Greek

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:29.280
Islands. They're charging a lot more

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:31.040
there." And she said, "Oh, but then I

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:33.200
have to go to this island to do the

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:34.760
driving test and do all of this stuff

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:36.240
and study." And I was just like, "Okay,

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:37.560
what Why don't you just go and take the

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:38.760
test?" And she said, "Oh, it's too much

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:40.520
for me to just deal with. I'd rather

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:41.839
just be comfortable here in Athens." And

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:43.480
I'm going to really get into this point

00:12:41.839 --> 00:12:44.720
later, but I want to be so gentle about

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:47.240
this first because I've had that

00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:49.920
mindset, too, at some point. Scarcity is

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:52.880
usually a learned survival tactic that

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:55.120
made sense at some point. But then, at

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:57.240
another given point, you know, sometime

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:59.600
further along, it will no longer serve

00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:01.080
you, especially if you want to build in

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:03.520
the long run, it really doesn't solve

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:05.640
any problems, and we're allowed to put

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:06.760
down that mindset. The question here is

00:13:05.640 --> 00:13:08.640
never about whether there's an

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:10.920
opportunity out there or not. There is

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:12.960
opportunity everywhere, but what are we

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:15.120
doing about it? Pillar one, your own

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:16.480
resources. So, here's what I came up

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:18.800
with for this video. I have four

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:21.000
pillars, and these decisions that I make

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:22.760
about building purpose and ambition

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:24.760
while also keeping my peace and my

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:26.800
freedom and doing whatever I want to do,

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:29.000
my softness, they all get run through

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:31.200
these pillars. So, number one, you must

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:33.760
have your own resources. You must have

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:35.600
your own money, your own accounts, you

00:13:33.760 --> 00:13:36.960
know, in your name, stuff in your name.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:39.040
I don't care how much you love your guy,

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.360
okay? I don't care how safe you're

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:41.400
feeling in a relationship or your

00:13:40.360 --> 00:13:42.840
marriage right now, or if you're

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:44.320
building a life together, and it feels

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:46.560
very, you know, maybe it feels very

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:48.800
unromantic to keep things separate for

00:13:46.560 --> 00:13:51.680
yourself. Nothing in your life should be

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:53.880
a single point of failure or a weak

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:56.560
link, because your life matters that

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:59.040
much. Even in my marriage of over 10

00:13:56.560 --> 00:14:00.920
years, we talk about this, and we can be

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:02.880
honest with each other about this. If a

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:05.120
relationship ends, you know, what would

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:06.920
that leave us with? If you have nothing

00:14:05.120 --> 00:14:09.160
of your name, then you do not have a

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:11.560
soft life. You have a very romantic

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:13.800
hostage situation. So, ask yourself

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:16.480
these questions very honestly, if this

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:17.720
relationship or this job ended tomorrow,

00:14:16.480 --> 00:14:20.080
or, you know, if I get cut off from my

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:22.760
family tomorrow, how many months can you

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:24.600
survive on money that is entirely yours?

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:27.000
Is your name on anything, an account, a

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:29.040
lease, an asset, business? Do you have

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:30.880
plans to put your name on anything? And

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:32.440
if not, are you going to have these

00:14:30.880 --> 00:14:34.680
plans? And lastly, [music]

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:37.560
do you have a skill set that you can

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:39.080
earn from within 30 days if you had to?

00:14:37.560 --> 00:14:41.400
Like, if the answer to any of these

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:43.400
things is no, that's not your fault, but

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:46.080
you get to make that your next project

00:14:43.400 --> 00:14:48.600
from now on. So, your first job is not

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:51.839
to be soft, not yet, but to become

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:53.920
untrappable. Pillar two, time is the

00:14:51.839 --> 00:14:56.400
only real currency. Most of us are

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:58.400
working way too hard for too many hours,

00:14:56.400 --> 00:15:00.320
and here's the brutal math that nobody

00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:02.440
wants to do, but I will do it for you,

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:04.920
because if you only earn by selling your

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:06.680
time and your hours, there is a hard

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:09.160
ceiling on your life, and you cannot

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:11.400
work more than 24 hours a day. I mean,

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:14.360
most of us can't work more than 16 or 18

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:16.440
hours. So, your income is capped past a

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:17.720
certain point, which means your freedom

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:19.800
is also capped, which means your

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:22.160
softness is also capped. And I'm saying

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:23.920
this as someone who has worked a lot

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:26.200
throughout my life and I worked many

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:28.840
jobs and sometimes I do work up to 18

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:30.440
hours and you know, I continue to work.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:33.480
But the difference between then and now

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:35.360
is now my income is no longer capped and

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:37.560
I basically learned how to use all the

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:40.520
money that I've earned from, you know,

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:42.720
giving my hours away in exchange for

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:45.280
building assets and over time over the

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:47.040
years, it has really helped me immensely

00:15:45.280 --> 00:15:49.320
and now I know from now on I can live a

00:15:47.040 --> 00:15:51.520
very comfortable life even if I choose

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:52.920
to not do anything tomorrow. And a lot

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:54.320
of people here in Europe actually will

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:56.040
look at the American tourist and they

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:57.560
will think, "Look at them having their

00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:59.680
Euro summer here. They have so much

00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:01.440
money and they're not working." On the

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:03.480
other hand, you know, a lot of people in

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:05.720
the US, they only get 2 weeks off every

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:07.200
year and they work 40 to 60 hours a week

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:09.360
and a lot of that 2 weeks is spent

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:11.280
visiting family and, you know, like

00:16:09.360 --> 00:16:13.680
doing things that they have to do. So,

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:15.240
what are we trading for exactly? A lot

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:17.120
of Europeans here have maybe like a

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:19.040
month or two off per year or more,

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:20.880
whereas Americans spend their 2 weeks to

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:22.440
experience this amazing quality of life

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:23.800
and eat real food, whereas the people

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:26.000
here may just be very indifferent to

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:27.120
that completely and spend their time

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.839
thinking about the things that they

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:30.320
lack. And if you spend your time

00:16:28.839 --> 00:16:32.240
thinking about what you don't have,

00:16:30.320 --> 00:16:34.120
whether it's us Americans looking at

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:36.240
like, "Wow, they have like amazing

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:38.120
quality of life that we don't have and

00:16:36.240 --> 00:16:39.880
they eat like, you know, amazing food

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:41.200
and fresh food, whatever." And then the

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:42.200
other hand, people here look at the

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:43.880
Americans and they're like, "Oh my god,

00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:45.520
they have so much money." Well, all of

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:47.720
these things, it's just such a waste of

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:49.360
time and in the grand scheme of things,

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:51.440
does it really matter? We don't have

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:52.960
that much time left. On one hand, we say

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:54.400
yes, we do have time and we still have

00:16:52.960 --> 00:16:56.640
the next time and there's still other

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:58.320
opportunities down the road, but I also

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.240
say that not to scare you, but to make

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:01.960
you like realize and wake up because

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:03.440
people will keep thinking that and keep

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:04.640
thinking like there's always more time,

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:06.600
there's always more time. One day,

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:08.720
they're going to wake up at 65 when they

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:10.760
retire and they realize, "I can't go on

00:17:08.720 --> 00:17:12.600
hikes anymore." So, we have to be really

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:14.880
honest with ourselves. Like you're going

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:16.400
to spend your one life someplace, you

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:18.760
know, wherever it is and the only

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:21.480
question is whether you design that for

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:23.040
yourself or whether you default into it

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:24.680
without even thinking about it, and just

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:26.880
there you are. Your whole life. Is that

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:28.400
what you really want? So, the goal is

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:31.000
not to work less. Again, that's like the

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:33.440
soft life fallacy talking. The goal is

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.640
to build things, projects that keep

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:37.760
producing crops for you after you stop

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:39.680
touching them. Like a farm, for example.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:41.160
Whatever it is, because trust me, this

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:43.400
is a whole other kind of worms, but

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:45.120
money is not that hard to make. And you

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:47.560
know, I made a lot of money while

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:49.040
working like hourly wages, like $15 an

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:52.040
hour. And I was able to do that through

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:54.360
making smart decisions, like trading and

00:17:52.040 --> 00:17:56.640
buying assets and really saving my money

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:59.040
and not going out and you know, spending

00:17:56.640 --> 00:18:01.280
like money on bottles and stuff. So,

00:17:59.040 --> 00:18:04.160
look at your income right now and label

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:07.200
every source as either rented or owned.

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:09.360
Rented means if you stop, it stops.

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:12.040
Whether it's your salary, your hourly

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:14.080
work, your client hours. Owned means it

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:16.360
continues. Whether that's a product that

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:18.040
you made, an asset, a business, a skill

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:20.400
that you've packaged. Something that

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:23.720
pays you while you sleep. Most people

00:18:20.400 --> 00:18:26.160
will have 100% rented everything,

00:18:23.720 --> 00:18:28.400
income, house, everything and zero

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:30.480
owned, which is completely fine. For

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:32.320
example, my house is rented, and when

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:34.440
I'm traveling, I am renting as well, but

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:36.520
that's not all I'm doing. I also own

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:38.160
properties, too, around the world. And

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:40.080
renting can make sense at different

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:42.080
times depending on the place and the

00:18:40.080 --> 00:18:43.440
opportunities that you have, more so

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:45.160
than owning something. So, you have to

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:46.960
be really smart about that, too. If you

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:49.040
don't have anything yet, this is the

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:50.640
perfect time to think about your future

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:52.680
and what you want to build for yourself.

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:54.520
Even if it's a skill set, getting better

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:57.040
at your craft, your art, your writing,

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:59.480
your academics. That is not rented, by

00:18:57.040 --> 00:19:01.400
the way. These skills, that is owned.

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:03.400
Skills that nobody can take away from

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:05.400
you. Knowledge. And I'm telling you this

00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:07.440
because even if you learn one skill, for

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:09.760
